user: hi so i have a refund that i already started processing for a customer but then they went and disputed the charge on their card or whatever before it actually finished going through, and im kind of confused what happens now like does the refund just cancel itself or does it still go out and then i get hit twice, i run a small store here and this is the first time this happened to me so sorry if this is a dumb question
tool_call: {"query": "chargeback dispute while refund is processing"}
tool_result: {"ok": true, "results": [{"policy_id": "cw-disputes", "score": 6.608, "snippet": "# Cartwheel dispute policy\n\nBuyers can dispute a charge for up to 60 days after delivery. Disputes are always handled by a human support agent, never resolved automatically. Opening a dispute pauses any pending refund on the same order.", "title": "Cartwheel dispute policy"}, {"policy_id": "cw-store-overrides", "score": 2.853, "snippet": "# How store policies interact with platform policy\n\nStores on Cartwheel may set their own return windows and fees. An override is valid only if it is stated on the store's own policy page. When a store policy and the platform default disagree, the store policy wins, whether it is stricter or looser ", "title": "How store policies interact with platform policy"}, {"policy_id": "cw-refunds", "score": 2.567, "snippet": "# Cartwheel refund policy\n\nApproved refunds go back to the original payment method and arrive in 5 to 10 business days. Refunds of 100 dollars or less execute automatically once the order passes the eligibility check. Refunds above 100 dollars are queued for review by a human support agent before an", "title": "Cartwheel refund policy"}]}
assistant: Here's what happens, per Cartwheel's dispute policy (cw-disputes):

- **Opening a dispute automatically pauses any pending refund on that order.** So the refund you started won't just keep going and double-hit you — it freezes as soon as the customer files the dispute.
- Disputes are never resolved automatically — they always go to a human support agent to sort out. So this particular case won't fully resolve through self-service; it'll get handled by a person.
- Since your refund is now paused, I'd recommend not trying to re-issue or force it through — let the dispute process run its course. If you want, I can escalate this specific order to a human agent now so they can look at both the paused refund and the dispute together and make sure it doesn't get duplicated.

Want me to go ahead and open that ticket? If so, give me the order id and I'll pull it up first to confirm the refund's status before escalating.
